The table gets κᶜ over 0–10 m beside 10–40 m; the figure gets κᶜ for both layers through time and
two rows of profiles (κᶜ and the TKE e, top 60 m, days 1, 2, 3, 5, 10, 20, 30), region means over
wet cells.

Why: the initial state is stable near the surface under ice (initial_stability.md: no unstable
faces in the top 10 m in the Beaufort Gyre and Central Arctic), yet the salty-surface /
fresh-below dipole is there in the first daily mean, with κᶜ at 10–40 m a hundred times background
on day 1. Is the top 10 m (two cells, 0–3.9 and 3.9–7.8 m) mixed through by the surface TKE on
day 1, or is the lens lost to the surface fluxes?

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AbhhvmHjZYCHhFxumZ9A47
